    },
    {
      "id": "claim_632e9d0a4e8c47faaf5597428f6afb70",
      "statement": "DUS-07 Section 4's cross-client confidentiality rule prohibits using information about one client's or counterparty's account behavior to generate content shown to a different client, even when presented as a pattern or typical value, which constrains any client-facing use of client_wire_history_features to the originating client's own aggregated history rather than beneficiary-side statistics pooled across unrelated clients.",
      "evidence": [
